local-changes:
  - renamed (DR-02, 2026-10-22): kit-core is core-kernel (@core/kernel), kit-web-core is core-web (@core/web), not core-core
    and core-web-core
  - all packages: dependency versions pinned to the DOC-11 versions (exact, no `^`; `@types/bun` and the others that were `latest`)
  - all packages: `exports` point at `src/*.ts` for the `bun`, `types` and `default` conditions (nothing is built or published, and
    Metro has no `bun` condition); `build` script, `files` and `tsconfig.build.json` removed; `test` script is
    `bun test --pass-with-no-tests` where the reference had none; version 0.0.0
  - core-runtime: `AppModule.privacy` and the `@core/privacy-participant` dependency removed (DR-03, DR-98)
  - core-http: `routes.ts` gains `IdParams`, `RouteSet`, `publicRoute`, `staffRoute` and `residentRoute`, so a module declares guard and
    audience in one spread (DOC-12 §5.3)
  - core-db: `Database.transaction()` added: begins a transaction, and inside an open one it is a savepoint; `run()` calls it
    when no transaction is open and still joins an open one (DOC-12 §8.1 items 1 and 2); test in `src/database.test.ts`
  - OpenTelemetry pinned to the 2.12 line (`@opentelemetry/api` 1.9.1, `resources` and `sdk-trace-node` 2.12.0,
    `exporter-trace-otlp-http` 0.223.0): `sdk-trace-node` 2.12.0 accepts `api` below 1.10 only (DOC-11 §3, §10)
  - core-kernel: the error classes of DOC-42 §4.1 (`ValidationError` with `details`, `RuleViolationError`, `PreconditionRequiredError`,
    `PayloadTooLargeError`, `UpgradeRequiredError`, `LockedError`, `RateLimitedError`, `UnavailableError`, `BadGatewayError`,
    `InvariantError`; `DomainError` carries `details` and `retryAfterSeconds`; `TooManyRequestsError` is `RateLimitedError`) (P1-04)
  - core-telemetry: `createLogger(level, { service, destination })`: ISO `time`, `level` as a word, `service`, redaction list,
    `err` serializer that keeps the SQLSTATE and drops the PostgreSQL `detail` (DOC-42 §8.3) (P1-04)
  - core-context: `RequestContext` carries `accountKind`, `accountId`, `role`, `buildingId`, `unitId` (P1-04)
  - core-http: `API_PREFIX` is `/api/v1`; the request id is a UUIDv7 and `[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}` (DOC-50 §5.1); the error handler is the
    answer of DOC-42 §3 (no `requestId` in the body, SQLSTATE mapping, `constraintErrors`, rule codes of DOC-42 §5.2); new
    `requestLogPlugin` (DOC-42 §8.1), `createClientIp`/`bucketIp` (DOC-39 §5.3), `corsPlugin` (replaces `@elysiajs/cors`, AG-25),
    `routePlugin` (`normalize: false`, AG-20) and `strictObject`; `maintenancePlugin` answers the shape of DOC-42 (P1-04)
  - core-runtime: `healthRoutes` is replaced by `readyRoute` and `liveRoute` (DOC-51 E-01, E-02: `ok`/`degraded`/`stopping`, checks with
    latency, the public path lists no dependency) (P1-04)
  - core-messaging: `OutboxRelay` takes `policy(type) -> { maxAttempts }`, `backoffBaseSeconds`, `backoffMaxSeconds`, `cleanupIntervalMs`
    and the sources carry their inbox (DR-118); the backoff, the dead-letter limit and the deferral budget are computed by the database
    clock in one UPDATE (DOC-38 §2.3); cleanup also deletes delivered inbox rows; `isFresh(maxAgeMs)`, `lastPassAt` and `sourceNames`;
    handler lines carry the message's correlation id as their request id; `DrizzleOutboxWriter` takes `OutboxRules` (the catalog
    of the module, the source, `buildingId`, the payload limit: JB-23, MC-05); new `OutboxAdmin` (list, requeue, discard dead
    letters); the zod `outboxConfig` slice is removed (the application builds `OutboxSettings` from DOC-41) (P1-05)
  - core-db: `Database.transaction(fn, { isolationLevel, accessMode })` for the `snapshot` jobs (P1-05)
  - core-runtime: `AppModule.jobs` is `JobDefinition[]` (not `ModuleJobs`); new `JobRuntime` (interval timers, the clock-job scheduler,
    `job_run` rows, `ctx.withLock`/`ctx.snapshot`, pause, stop with a timeout, `runNow`), `schedule.ts` (`lastSlot`, `decide`),
    `SqlJobRunStore`; `createRuntime` takes the relay settings, the manifests (for `outboxPolicies`) and the job settings and
    returns `relayCheck`, `startWorker`, `stopWorker`; `intervalJobs`/`noJobs` are removed (P1-05)
  - core-runtime: `db-cli.ts` (the reference's db:generate/db:migrate), `cluster.ts` (process supervisor) and `maintenance-config.ts` (a zod slice)
    are removed: `scripts/migrate.ts` and `scripts/db.ts` run the migrations of this project (DOC-19 §3.1), the scaling unit is the
    container (DOC-41 `APP_PROCESSES`) and the key is in `apps/api/src/bootstrap/config` (P1-06)
  - core-kernel: `SecretBox` (`seal`, `open`, `newestKeyId`, `createSecretBox`, `keyRingFromBase64`): AES-256-GCM envelope
    `v1:<keyId>:<iv>:<ciphertext+tag>` with the AAD bound to the row (DOC-36 §6, DR-126); `RuleViolationError` takes an optional
    answer `code` (default `validation_failed`) for the rules the catalog names (`file_not_verified`) (P1-07)
  - core-context: `RequestContext.ip` and `userAgent`, set by the new core-http `clientInfoPlugin` and read by `AuditApi.record`
    (DOC-35 §3.2); core-runtime: `ModuleManifest.auditActions`, the actions a module may write (DOC-35 §3.3) (P1-08)
  - core-storage: `ObjectStorage.readRange` (a ranged GET for the first 4 KB of an upload), `writeStream` (a multipart upload from a
    stream) and `presignGet(key, ttl, { downloadName })` (`response-content-disposition`), in the S3 and local adapters, the fake
    and the contract test (DOC-37 §6.3, §8, §9) (P1-07)
  - core-db: `inBuilding(table, scope)`, the typed predicate of the building scope (DOC-12 §7.2); the scope type is structural
    because a core package may not import `@rms/shared-types` (P1-07)
  - core-kernel: `requireRole(actor, allowed)`, the role gate of a use case: 403 `forbidden` unless `actor.role` is listed (DOC-12 §5.3, §14
    item 3); test in `src/require-role.test.ts`
  - core-i18n: the catalog lookup walks own keys only (`Object.hasOwn`), so `__proto__` and inherited keys resolve to nothing (Semgrep, P1-10)
  - core-kernel: `Transition<S>`, `decide` and `MAX_DECIDE_ATTEMPTS`: an aggregate returns the state change it decided, a repository applies it in one
    guarded statement, and `decide` loads and decides again when the statement lost a race (DR-255); test in `src/transition.test.ts`
  - core-db: `applyTransition(database, table, transition, { stamp, also })`, the one guarded `UPDATE … SET <set> WHERE id AND <expect> RETURNING *`
    that applies a kernel `Transition` (DR-255); timestamps compare at millisecond precision
  - core-http: `createIdempotent(store, clock)` and `noIdempotency`, the wrapper of DOC-50 §8 for a route marked `R` (the key row, the replay of a stored
    2xx with `Idempotent-Replayed`, 422 `idempotency_key_reuse`, the `external` mode with 409 `request_in_progress` and the takeover of a dead key
    after five minutes), with `requestHash` and `canonicalJson`; `staffRoute`'s `extra` carries `idempotent: true`; core-db: `SqlIdempotencyStore`,
    its adapter on `platform.idempotency_key`, matched to the core-http `IdempotencyStore` by shape because a core package may not import
    another that is not listed for it (P1-28, DR-259); tests in `idempotency.test.ts`
  - core-http: every route helper takes a required `RouteInfo` (`endpoint` E-xx, `operationId`, `idempotent`, `stepUp`, `byPurpose`, `credential`) and writes it
    as `operationId`, `x-endpoint-id`, `x-audience`, `x-idempotent` and `x-step-up` of the operation, so the authorization-matrix generator and test AG-02 join the
    mounted routes with DOC-51 §2; `idempotent` and `stepUp` leave `x-audience`, where they were `extra` (P1-15); core-runtime: `readyRoute` carries the same
    record for E-02
  - core-http: `RouteInfo` takes a required `summary` and an optional `description`, written as the same keys of the operation (the name and the text of the
    endpoint in the API reference); `describedEnum(values, description?)` is a string enum whose OpenAPI schema carries the meaning of each value
    (`x-enumDescriptions` and a Markdown list), as Elysia's `UnionEnum` kind because the OpenAPI plugin drops the description of a union of literals; the
    error handler reports a value outside it as the rule `enum` with the allowed values; test in `error-handler.plugin.test.ts`; core-runtime: `readyRoute`
    describes its 503 `status` the same way (AG-02a, AG-02b)
  - core-http: `strictObject(properties, { description })` takes the description of the object; `IdParams.id` has a description (AG-02c)
  - core-db: `Database.poolWaiting`, the top-level transactions in flight beyond the pool size, for `db_pool_waiting` (DOC-40 §4.1) (P1-18)
  - core-telemetry: `Metrics` over `prom-client` 15.1.3 (counter, gauge, histogram, `pulled` gauges with a cache, a timeout and no series before the first read, the two process metrics, `render`); `prom-client` is a dependency (P1-18)
  - core-http: `requestLogPlugin` takes `observe(sample)`, called once per request with the route template, status, error code, the scope of a 429 and the app headers; `createIdempotent` takes `onOutcome(first|replay|reuse|in_progress)` (P1-18)
  - core-messaging: `InProcessMessageBus` takes `observe(handler, outcome)`; new `OutboxStats` (oldest unpublished age and dead letters per source) (P1-18)
  - core-runtime: `createRuntime` takes `onHandler`; `AppModule.gauges` (`ModuleGauge`): gauges a module reads from its own tables at a scrape (P1-18)
  - core-db: `GaplessCounter` (`createGaplessCounter` / `SqlGaplessCounter.next`), the `document_counter` upsert of DOC-12 §9.5 in the caller's ambient transaction with `updated_at = now()`, refused outside a transaction (DR-10, DOC-14 §10) (P2-02)
  - core-runtime: `SqlJobRunStore.lastSuccessDetails(name)`, the `details` of the latest succeeded run of a job, for the gauge `ledger_invariant_violations` (P2-11)
